     "id": "03f5v9zjw7pz8717a4no1h8a7",
     "name": "David Heinemeier Hansson",
@@ -156,6 +161,36 @@ __Response:__
 
 Returns `204 No Content` on success.
 
+## Board Publication
+
+Only account admins (including owners) with access to a board can publish or unpublish it. Creating a board does not grant a non-admin permission to publish it. Publication does not change the board's account membership or `all_access` setting.
+
+### `POST /:account_slug/boards/:board_id/publication`
+
+Publishes the board and returns `201 Created` with no response body. No parameters are required. Fetch the board's JSON to obtain its `public_url`.
+
+Publishing an already-published board preserves its URL.
+
+### `DELETE /:account_slug/boards/:board_id/publication`
+
+Unpublishes the board and returns `204 No Content`. The public board URL and its column and card URLs immediately stop working. This request also succeeds if the board is already unpublished.
+
+Publishing the board again creates a new secret URL; the old URL remains invalid.
+
+### Public pages
+
+Anyone with the secret key can open these read-only HTML pages without signing in:
+
+- `GET /:account_slug/public/boards/:key`
+- `GET /:account_slug/public/boards/:key/columns/:id`
+- `GET /:account_slug/public/boards/:key/cards/:number`
+
+The key also works at `/public/boards/:key` (and its nested column and card paths) without an account prefix. If an account prefix is supplied, it must match the published board's account.
+
+Only published cards are visible, including their descriptions, steps, and comments. Drafts and cards or columns from other boards are not exposed. Column pages show active published cards, while the board page and direct card URLs also include done and postponed cards.
+
+Unknown or revoked keys, inaccessible columns, and unpublished cards return `404 Not Found`. Keep the URL private unless you intend to share the board's contents.
+
 ## Board Accesses
 
 Board accesses let you see who has access to a board and their involvement level (watching or access only). Any board member can view this information.
